.docname {Configuration}
.include {docs}

The board layout and the behavior probabilities live in a single TOML file that
both front ends read and write.

## File location

```text
${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/creature_life_cycle/simulation.toml
```

With the default environment, that is
`~/.config/creature_life_cycle/simulation.toml`.

If the file is missing, the program creates it from built-in standard board
data and default behavior parameters. If it exists but is invalid, the program
loads those defaults **without overwriting the file**, so a typo never costs
you your setup.

The repository ships .repolink {simulation.example.toml} {blob/main/simulation.example.toml},
which mirrors the built-in defaults.

## Example

```toml
[board]
rows = 10
columns = 10

aphids = [
  { x = 3, y = 5 },
  { x = 4, y = 8 },
]

ladybugs = [
  { x = 5, y = 9 },
  { x = 1, y = 1 },
]

[aphid]
move_probability = 0.7
kill_probability = 0.2
accomplice_probability = 0.1
procreation_probability = 0.4

[ladybug]
move_probability = 0.7
kill_probability = 0.2
direction_change_probability = 0.4
procreation_probability = 0.2

[food]
regeneration_probability = 0.1
```

## `[board]`

| Key | Type | Description |
|-----|------|-------------|
| `rows` | integer | Board height; must be greater than zero |
| `columns` | integer | Board width; must be greater than zero |
| `aphids` | array of `{ x, y }` | Starting aphid positions |
| `ladybugs` | array of `{ x, y }` | Starting ladybug positions |

Coordinates are zero-based: `x` is the row and `y` is the column. Positions
outside the board are skipped with a warning rather than rejected.

Starting aphids have `10` life and starting ladybugs have `15` life. Each cell
starts with a random food value from `0` through `9`.

## `[aphid]`

| Key | Default | Meaning |
|-----|---------|---------|
| `move_probability` | `0.7` | Chance the aphid moves during the movement phase |
| `kill_probability` | `0.2` | Base chance of killing a ladybug in the same cell |
| `accomplice_probability` | `0.1` | Extra kill chance per other aphid in the cell |
| `procreation_probability` | `0.4` | Chance of producing a child when sharing a cell |

## `[ladybug]`

| Key | Default | Meaning |
|-----|---------|---------|
| `move_probability` | `0.7` | Chance the ladybug moves during the movement phase |
| `kill_probability` | `0.2` | Chance of killing an aphid in the same cell |
| `direction_change_probability` | `0.4` | Chance of picking a new preferred direction set |
| `procreation_probability` | `0.2` | Chance of producing a child when sharing a cell |

## `[food]`

| Key | Default | Meaning |
|-----|---------|---------|
| `regeneration_probability` | `0.1` | Chance a cell below the cap regains one food after a turn |

Food is capped at `9` per cell and never drops below `0`.

## Validation

- `rows` and `columns` must both be greater than zero.
- All probability values must be from `0.0` through `1.0`.
- The `[aphid]`, `[ladybug]`, and `[food]` sections are optional. An omitted
  section falls back to its default probabilities.
- Creature positions outside the board are skipped with a warning.

> Warning: An invalid file is not repaired automatically. The run continues on
> built-in defaults, and your file stays exactly as written so you can fix it.

## Saving from the GUI

**Save setup** in the GUI's Overview tab (.keybinding {S}) writes the current
creature positions and probabilities back to this same file, creating parent
directories as needed. Food values, creature life values, and the current turn
are not saved. See [Graphical interface](gui.qd) for the surrounding controls.
